    "body": "fix on issue/33-continuous-c · PR #286 (draft, `Refs #33`) · pinned by c_axis_live::{a_rotary_contour_on_the_spindle_states_c_on_every_move_and_posts, the_wrapped_helix_posts_to_its_golden, every_post_without_c_or_without_the_machines_words_refuses_by_name, the_c_word_rides_the_stream_and_parses_back}, rotary_letter::the_mill_turn_spindle_as_c_axis_answers_c_and_stamps_it, cl::rotary::tests (3) · merges at the next cut\n\nFirst slice. On a mill-turn's spindle C, Rotary Contour/Parallel/Offset now generate, verify and post:\n- `cl::Move::rotary` holds the stated, unwrapped C. `cl::stamp_c` splits each move until the machine's C-linear motion follows the verified chord to the op's tolerance.\n- The letter gate admits C, and `check_document` reads the stated C.\n- The stream carries `PARAM LiveTool` and `C`. The engine refuses that section for scripts without `liveTooling`, which covers every mill post.\n- fanuc-lathe.cps writes `G01 X(dia) Z C` under G98. It uses the machine's new `tool_station.live_tool` words and refuses by name when they are absent.\n\nGate: the touched suites are green (cl, post, app c_axis_live/rotary_letter/conformance/fanuc_post/golden_cl/lathe_*/machine/posting/project_roundtrip/post_not_judged/rotary_*/tormach_*/turning, 18 binaries). clippy -D warnings is clean on cl/post/motion/sim/app/ui. The sim/motion/ui edits are mechanical `rotary: None` literal fields: compiled and clippy-checked, not run.\n\nStill owed on this issue (docs/decisions/33-continuous-c.md):\n1. A machine C-sense word.\n2. Unwinding C on links against a stated travel. The shipped millturn.mch states -360..360, so a multi-ring path is refused by the letter gate.\n3. Axial/face live-tool stations and G12.1 polar interpolation.\n4. Arcs on a C turn.\n5. Confirming the composite (degree-as-mm) rotary feed law on a real control.\n6. live_tool words in a shipped machine. None is stated, so in-app posting refuses by name until the user's .mch states its builder's codes.\n",
