    "body": "review round 1 fixed on issue/33-c-unwind · PR #860 head 5c582cd5 (still a draft) · merges at the next cut\n\n- Rotary Parallel and Rotary Offset: took the refusal path. They do not unwind. On a stated C travel they post only what fits as stamped, as before this PR, and are refused by name where C would need a rewind. Pinned by operation::rotary_gate::tests::parallel_and_offset_are_refused_by_name_where_c_would_need_a_rewind. Why there are no end-to-end tests is in docs/decisions/33-c-unwind.md.\n- Rewind feed: fanuc-lathe.cps caps every C block's composite F so the X/Z part stays within the machine's stated feed and the C part within its stated C rate. Where no C rate is stated, C is uncapped (the rate is unbounded by data on such a machine). The unwind golden's orbit now posts F6000, was F22954; the retract posts F4000. Pinned by c_axis_unwind::a_lower_stated_rate_posts_a_lower_feed and a read-back check on every posted C block. No existing golden moved (c_axis_helix.nc is byte-identical).\n- unwind_c now refuses a non-finite point and a broken chain by name (two new unit tests).\n\nGate on the final head, with main bdd29e00 merged in: quick tier, which fell back to batch for the cl change. All 9 steps green, including clippy -D warnings.",
