    "body": "review round 2 fixed on issue/33-c-unwind · PR #860 head ff0fb392 (still a draft) · merges at the next cut\n\n- The radial-clearance link in unwind_c is now opt-in, and off for Rotary Contour, the only kind that unwinds. The contour's links are always the axial clearance plane, and no op parameter makes them radial, so no shipped op reaches the radial branch. A contour stretch whose only clear point is radial is refused by name.\n- The radial branch is pinned by its own unit tests:\n  - a_radial_link_beyond_the_cut_unwinds_at_its_radius_when_admitted\n  - a_radial_link_at_or_inside_the_cut_radius_is_no_link\n  - a_radial_only_link_is_refused_by_name_where_radial_links_are_not_admitted\n- The wiring is pinned by rotary_gate::tests::the_contour_takes_no_radial_link.\n- PR body: the Parallel/Offset gap is stated as closed by refusal (they never unwind), and the real-control items are still listed as owed.\n\nGate on the final head, with main 4c3f7565 merged in: quick tier, which fell back to batch for the cl change. All 9 steps green, including clippy -D warnings.",
